amp`. ","Correct, because all IndexableField instances would count also points, which by default is always the case. "],"path":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/DataStreamTimestampFieldMapper.java","id":36736,"created_at":"2024-07-08T18:25:52Z","original_position":40,"side":"LEFT","position":68,"submitted_on_commit":"ed3477b9158052287f0b53585d7c41db242ea7fc","diff_hunk":"@@ -195,37 +195,25 @@ public void postParse(DocumentParserContext context) throws IOException {\n             // not configured, so skip the validation\n             return;\n         }\n-        boolean foundFsTimestampField \u003d false;\n-        IndexableField first \u003d null;\n-        final List\u003cIndexableField\u003e fields \u003d context.rootDoc().getFields();\n-        for (int i \u003d 0; i \u003c fields.size(); i++) {\n-            IndexableField indexableField \u003d fields.get(i);\n-            if (DEFAULT_PATH.equals(indexableField.name()) \u003d\u003d false) {\n-                continue;\n-            }\n-            if (first \u003d\u003d null) {\n-                first \u003d indexableField;\n-            }\n-            if (indexableField.fieldType().docValuesType() \u003d\u003d DocValuesType.SORTED_NUMERIC) {","submitted_line":209},"generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"Introduce new constants and modify methods to use these constants for timestamp handling. Ensure that the introduction of `TIMESTAMP_VALUE_KEY` and `TIMESTAMP_MULTIPLE_VALUES_FLAG` is consistent across all relevant parts of the code. Verify that the usage of these keys does not introduce any unintended side effects, especially in scenarios where multiple fields or documents are processed.","nodes":[{"id":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/DataStreamTimestampFieldMapper.java-server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/DataStreamTimestampFieldMapper.java-8348:8386,8410:8415,8418:8422,8432:8498,8507:9170,9184:9189,9555:9560-8459:8477,8480:8534,8544:8717,8727:8808,8821:8